{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490325-v20-tremere-with-mage-familiars","id":1490325,"title":"V20-Tremere With Mage Familiars?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-15T18:16:39-07:00","id":1490325,"title":"V20-Tremere With Mage Familiars?","content":"So,the concept of a vampire ghouling a mage to have a powerful servant is one that has been discussed on some mta and vtm books. But few books shined a spotlight on it, one of them is the v20 tal'mahe'ra book. Which has a group of vampires that has a Combination Discipline &quot;Chain The Enlightened&quot; to bind a a Mage to him forever. As well as a spell for a mage to give himself to a vampire as a bound partner<br /> wanna know something fun?<br /> the afore mentioned Combination Discipline is Dominate 6 Auspex 5,meaning a whole lot of Tremere might or at least have the potential to know it,and let's nor forget that the order of Hermes hates the tremere now more than ever. So,I'd like to do this fun thought exercise, do you think a tremere can learn the Combination Discipline without talking or even knowing about the tal'mahe'ra? I personally think the Tremere are across all editions,hard-core camarilla members as a whole. So i can't very well see them learning from any other Sect,but I must ask if we assume for thr sake of the argument a Combination Discipline can he learned without a teacher? Do you think there's tremere out here with Thaumaturgy and True Magick?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T18:38:13-07:00","id":1490330,"title":"","content":"Better fun<br /> <br /> It has been stated in the past that with the right combination of sphere scores a mage can turn a vampire permanently back into a mortal, regardless of Generation or age. Following that, it would mean that a similar set of spheres would allow a mage to enhance the vampire in the other direction. All it would take is one pet mage with the right scores to make an entire clan 2nd or 3rd generation vampires.<br /> <br /> That feels a little more Tremere-esque to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T18:46:55-07:00","id":1490331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490325-v20-tremere-with-mage-familiars?p=1490330#post1490330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Better fun<br /> <br /> It has been stated in the past that with the right combination of sphere scores a mage can turn a vampire permanently back into a mortal, regardless of Generation or age. Following that, it would mean that a similar set of spheres would allow a mage to enhance the vampire in the other direction. All it would take is one pet mage with the right scores to make an entire clan 2nd or 3rd generation vampires.<br /> <br /> That feels a little more Tremere-esque to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>My oh my this potential crossover is getting more appealing by the moment.<br /> Do you imagine hermetics and their mage friends raid tremere chantries very often?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T23:25:59-07:00","id":1490352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490325-v20-tremere-with-mage-familiars?p=1490331#post1490331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you imagine hermetics and their mage friends raid tremere chantries very often?</div> </div> </div> </div>Since the Tremere are technically ex-hermetics, I could see some back-channel diplomacy going on while an official stance is more antagonistic.<br /> <br /> Though with a specialization in Forces, even the most inexperienced hermetic should be able to produce sunlight on demand, so I would think there has to be a reason why the mages have not purged vampires in general. The Technocracy could easily swap out normal light bulbs for sunlight producing ones and no one would know the difference until the streetlamps came on.<br /> <br /> So with those things in mind, you will pretty much have to home brew reasons why mages don't destroy vampires. The Technocracy taking down an Antediluvian shows the power disparity, especially when you consider the implications of Arch Mages potentially existing.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T04:44:11-07:00","id":1490370,"title":"","content":"Ghouling tends to damage a mages ability to use sphere magic. Blood treachery explored this issue length, i think it would initially work but the mages powers would slowly diminish until you got a bog standard ghoul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T06:01:51-07:00","id":1490379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490325-v20-tremere-with-mage-familiars?p=1490370#post1490370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghouling tends to damage a mages ability to use sphere magic. Blood treachery explored this issue length, i think it would initially work but the mages powers would slowly diminish until you got a bog standard ghoul.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood Treachery rules have been declared as optional in M20 (BoS). Personaly, I'm not a fan of those rules, so I'm happy about that door being open, or half open anyway.<br /> <br /> The one &quot;damage&quot; to Spheres that it's consistent trough editions (and also the Black Hand) it's that mages can't raise their Arete (and spheres?, I don't remember that one) while they're Ghouls. So, unless you bonded an Archmaster somehow, you will have a rather weak mage forever (and there go the dreams of reaching Caine trough \u00fcber-magicks :P), unless you accept to &quot;starve&quot; your mage until they can raise their power a little more, from time to time...<br /> <br /> ...for the tal'mahe'ra this works because their mages worshipp vampires, and take this as a sort of ritual fasting to become more enligthened (which, to be fair, it's exactly what it is).<br /> <br /> It could be a problem if your mage counts on being a Ghoul to stave off aging, but maybe a temporary spell to stop aging could be enacted just for the period of fasting, &quot;Permanent&quot; Paradox for that kind of work goes away when the spell ends and Ghouldom resumes.<br /> <br /> Also: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490038-mages-and-ghouldom/page2\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ghouldom/page2</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 08-16-2022, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T06:50:48-07:00","id":1490382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490325-v20-tremere-with-mage-familiars?p=1490352#post1490352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the Tremere are technically ex-hermetics, I could see some back-channel diplomacy going on while an official stance is more antagonistic.</div> </div> </div> </div>AFAIK this is canon, actually. They always have at least one House they keep in contact with.<br /> <br /> Even when the Tremere got caught as vampires in the Middle Ages the Order took years to decided to expel them. Not just to declare war, but for some years the Tremere were vampires <b>and</b> members of the Order of Hermes. So even back then their stance wasn't really that drastic. Imagine today.<br /> <br /> I don't think the fact Mages are so superior in direct confrontation means it's so hard to picture a war not being so simple for them to win. Between hiding, backstabbing, ambushes, traps and all the things that can go back and forth in a war, obliterating their enemy isn't that simple even if they really want to do that. The effort and cost would be huge in any such attempt for global-spanning absolute genocide. And vampires are masters in... making compromises so this effort isn't really necessary. That's already why the Technocracy doesn't try.<br /> <br /> For the &quot;Mage Familiars&quot;, I don't think that would go widespread. We could have three possible situations: hostages, traitors and liaisons to the Tremere. Hostages would be the rarest of them all, a Tremere manages to Ghoul a member of the Order for the purpose of using them as a bargaining chip. That's too tricky to work frequently, but would justify some Tremere being able to avoid the more belligerent Hermetics. Traitors would be your &quot;typical&quot; deal as far as it goes, the vampire Ghouls a Mage and both keep that a secret, so at the very least the Order of Hermes, but probably also Clan Tremere, are none the wiser. Finally the liaisons would be selected Mages deemed to be useful among the Tremere, so they can report, act as diplomats, even conduct vampire-related research alongside the Tremere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T07:54:08-07:00","id":1490396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490325-v20-tremere-with-mage-familiars?p=1490379#post1490379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Blood Treachery rules have been declared as optional in M20 (BoS). Personaly, I'm not a fan of those rules, so I'm happy about that door being open, or half open anyway.<br /> <br /> The one &quot;damage&quot; to Spheres that it's consistent trough editions (and also the Black Hand) it's that mages can't raise their Arete (and spheres?, I don't remember that one) while they're Ghouls. So, unless you bonded an Archmaster somehow, you will have a rather weak mage forever (and there go the dreams of reaching Caine trough \u00fcber-magicks :P), unless you accept to &quot;starve&quot; your mage until they can raise their power a little more, from time to time...<br /> <br /> ...for the tal'mahe'ra this works because their mages worshipp vampires, and take this as a sort of ritual fasting to become more enligthened (which, to be fair, it's exactly what it is).<br /> <br /> It could be a problem if your mage counts on being a Ghoul to stave off aging, but maybe a temporary spell to stop aging could be enacted just for the period of fasting, &quot;Permanent&quot; Paradox for that kind of work goes away when the spell ends and Ghouldom resumes.<br /> <br /> Also: <a href=\"http://&quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1490038-mages-and-ghouldom/page2&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...ghouldom/page2</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Surprising, thematically it actually makes sense being ghouled would wreck a mage. Being mages and ghouls are diametrically opposed in same sense as say a hellos aligned fera abomination.<br /> <br /> If it didn't wreck a mages ability to casting case I suspect it'd eventually end in the death of tremere due to sheer range of risks of ghouling a mage.<br /> <br /> I could see it working with tremere raised sorcerors however","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 08-16-2022, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T11:25:47-07:00","id":1490411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490325-v20-tremere-with-mage-familiars#post1490325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So,the concept of a vampire ghouling a mage to have a powerful servant is one that has been discussed on some mta and vtm books. But few books shined a spotlight on it, one of them is the v20 tal'mahe'ra book. Which has a group of vampires that has a Combination Discipline &quot;Chain The Enlightened&quot; to bind a a Mage to him forever. As well as a spell for a mage to give himself to a vampire as a bound partner<br /> wanna know something fun?<br /> the afore mentioned Combination Discipline is Dominate 6 Auspex 5,meaning a whole lot of Tremere might or at least have the potential to know it,and let's nor forget that the order of Hermes hates the tremere now more than ever. So,I'd like to do this fun thought exercise, do you think a tremere can learn the Combination Discipline without talking or even knowing about the tal'mahe'ra? I personally think the Tremere are across all editions,hard-core camarilla members as a whole. So i can't very well see them learning from any other Sect,but I must ask if we assume for thr sake of the argument a Combination Discipline can he learned without a teacher? Do you think there's tremere out here with Thaumaturgy and True Magick?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have a friend ST who used a similar concept in one of his games. In his games the power (<i>Chain the Enlightened </i>) wasn't developed by the Tal'Mahe'Ra (he didn't like them very much), but rather the Tremere Inner Council, and it was like a top secret of the clan and only the Councillors (and naturally Tremere himself) knew about it Basically, he kind of imported the concept of Tremere Liches from Awakening to the WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T13:38:33-07:00","id":1490436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490325-v20-tremere-with-mage-familiars?p=1490411#post1490411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I have a friend ST who used a similar concept in one of his games. In his games the power (<i>Chain the Enlightened </i>) wasn't developed by the Tal'Mahe'Ra (he didn't like them very much), but rather the Tremere Inner Council, and it was like a top secret of the clan and only the Councillors (and naturally Tremere himself) knew about it Basically, he kind of imported the concept of Tremere Liches from Awakening to the WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really great! Did your st had any Tremere with a Blood Familiar show up in game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T13:40:23-07:00","id":1490437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490325-v20-tremere-with-mage-familiars?p=1490382#post1490382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AFAIK this is canon, actually. They always have at least one House they keep in contact with.<br /> <br /> Even when the Tremere got caught as vampires in the Middle Ages the Order took years to decided to expel them. Not just to declare war, but for some years the Tremere were vampires <b>and</b> members of the Order of Hermes. So even back then their stance wasn't really that drastic. Imagine today.<br /> <br /> I don't think the fact Mages are so superior in direct confrontation means it's so hard to picture a war not being so simple for them to win. Between hiding, backstabbing, ambushes, traps and all the things that can go back and forth in a war, obliterating their enemy isn't that simple even if they really want to do that. The effort and cost would be huge in any such attempt for global-spanning absolute genocide. And vampires are masters in... making compromises so this effort isn't really necessary. That's already why the Technocracy doesn't try.<br /> <br /> For the &amp;quot;Mage Familiars&amp;quot;, I don't think that would go widespread. We could have three possible situations: hostages, traitors and liaisons to the Tremere. Hostages would be the rarest of them all, a Tremere manages to Ghoul a member of the Order for the purpose of using them as a bargaining chip. That's too tricky to work frequently, but would justify some Tremere being able to avoid the more belligerent Hermetics. Traitors would be your &amp;quot;typical&amp;quot; deal as far as it goes, the vampire Ghouls a Mage and both keep that a secret, so at the very least the Order of Hermes, but probably also Clan Tremere, are none the wiser. Finally the liaisons would be selected Mages deemed to be useful among the Tremere, so they can report, act as diplomats, even conduct vampire-related research alongside the Tremere.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree monteparnas<br /> Honestly I think if the order of Hermes and their allies fought the tremere and their allies, it'd a coin toss to e who wins","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T15:53:06-07:00","id":1490448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490325-v20-tremere-with-mage-familiars?p=1490436#post1490436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's really great! Did your st had any Tremere with a Blood Familiar show up in game?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, quite often in fact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}